# Template for the isolated testbed group. Copy to <group>.txt using the exact
# group= value from your inventory. See compute.example for the gitignore rule.

# NAME THIS FILE FOR THE TARGET ROLE, NEVER FOR THE CONSOLE LABEL.
#
# Cloud object names drift independently: a VPC rename may be API-able while the
# matching subnet and NAT gateway updates are console-only, so an estate in a
# MIXED naming state is normal and expected. Group files key on SSH aliases, and
# aliases are built from port + IP, so a cloud rename cannot break them. Terraform
# is likewise unaffected when it references networks by ID rather than by name --
# verify that in your own stack before assuming it.
#
# Do not "fix" the stale labels by guessing. Describe the mixed state plainly and
# list each place the old string appears, sorted into:
#   (a) safe to change now      -- prose describing the network as it is today
#   (b) must wait for the rename -- consumers that resolve the name at runtime
#   (c) historical, keep         -- dated results, finished reports, log paths
# Beware a substring that merely LOOKS like the old label (a domain, a job name):
# sweeping on the short word rewrites the wrong strings. Sweep on the full
# object tokens instead.

cluster-testbed-server-1
cluster-testbed-server-2
cluster-testbed-agent-1

# Single-node canary used for create/destroy experiments on the same entry.
canary-alias
